.TH "UNIDESK" "1" "2022-03-25"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
unidesk -- UniDeskBrowser remote desktop client
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
unidesk [-a|i|n|q|v] [-c FILE] [-e FILE] [-p TABINDEX] [-s SERVER]
[-t PROTOCOL] [-x PLUGIN] [--update-profile]
[--set-option OPTION[=VALUE]] [--display DISPLAY]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
UniDeskBrowser is a remote desktop client written in GTK+, based on Remmina.\& It
aims to be useful for system administrators and travellers, who need to work
with lots of remote computers in front of either large monitors or tiny
netbooks.\& UniDeskBrowser supports multiple network protocols in an integrated and
consistent user interface, with all connections in a single window.\&
.PP
Currently RDP, SSH, SFTP and TELNET are supported.\&
.PP
UniDeskBrowser is free and open-source software, released under GNU GPL license.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
${XDG_CONFIG_DIRS}/unidesk/unidesk.\&pref or ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/unidesk/unidesk.\&pref :
.PP
UniDeskBrowser configuration files.\&
.PP
At the first UniDeskBrowser execution the system wide UniDeskBrowser configuration files,
will be copied in the ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}
.PP
${XDG_DATA_HOME}/unidesk :
.PP
UniDeskBrowser data folder with the connection database.\& Legacy Remmina profiles
(${XDG_DATA_HOME}/remmina/FILE.\&remmina) are imported once at the first start.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Show help options
.PP
.RE
\fB-a\fR
.RS 4
Show about dialog
.PP
.RE
\fB-c, --connect=FILE\fR
.RS 4
Connect directly either to a desktop using options described in a file,
or a supported URI (RDP, SSH or TELNET).\&
.br
The filetype can be ".\&remmina" or one supported by a plugin capable of
importing files
.PP
.RE
\fB-e, --edit=FILE\fR
.RS 4
Open and edit desktop connection using options described by file,
file type can be either .\&remmina or one supported by a file
import capable plugin
.PP
.RE
\fB-n, --new\fR
.RS 4
Create a new connection profile
.PP
.RE
\fB-p, --pref=TABINDEX\fR
.RS 4
Show preferences dialog page
.PP
.RE
\fB-x, --plugin=PLUGIN\fR
.RS 4
Execute the plugin
.PP
.RE
\fB-q, --quit\fR
.RS 4
Quit the application
.PP
.RE
\fB-s, --server=SERVER\fR
.RS 4
Use default server name (for \fB--new\fR)
.PP
.RE
\fB-t, --protocol=PROTOCOL\fR
.RS 4
Use default protocol (for \fB--new\fR)
.PP
.RE
\fB-i, --icon\fR
.RS 4
Start as tray icon
.PP
.RE
\fB-v, --version\fR
.RS 4
Show the application'\&s version
.PP
.RE
\fB--update-profile\fR
.RS 4
Modify connection profile, require also \fB--set-option\fR
.PP
.RE
\fB--set-option OPTION[=VALUE]\fR
.RS 4
Set one or more profile settings, to be used with \fB--update-pro-file\fR
.PP
.RE
\fB--encrypt-password\fR
.RS 4
Encrypt a password
.PP
.RE
\fB--display=DISPLAY\fR
.RS 4
X display to use
.PP
.RE
\fB--disable-toolbar\fR
.RS 4
Disable toolbar
.PP
.RE
\fB--enable-fullscreen\fR
.RS 4
Enable fullscreen
.PP
.RE
\fB--enable-extra-hardening\fR
.RS 4
Enable extra hardening (disable closing confirmation, disable unsafe shortcut keys, hide tabs, hide search bar)
.br
List of disabled shortcut keys:
.br
fullscreen, autofit, prevtab and nexttab, scale, grab, minimize, viewonly, screenshot, disconnect, toolbar
.PP
.RE
\fB--no-tray-icon\fR
.RS 4
Disable tray icon
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
To connect using an exisitng connection profile use:
\fBunidesk -c FILE.\&remmina\fR
.PP
To quick connect using a URI:
.PP
unidesk -c rdp://username@server
.br
unidesk -c rdp://domain\\\\username@server
.br
unidesk -c ssh://user@server
.br
unidesk -c telnet://user@server
.PP
To quick connect using a URI along with an encrypted password:
.PP
unidesk -c rdp://username:encrypted-password@server
.PP
To encrypt a password for use with a URI:
.PP
unidesk --encrypt-password
.PP
To update username and password and set a different resolution mode of a
UniDeskBrowser connection profile use:
.PP
echo "ausernamenapassword" | unidesk --update-profile /PATH/TO/FOO.\&remmina --set-option username --set-option resolution_mode=2 --set-option password
.PP
